From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Updates menu: DUCKTALE NIGHTLIES updater + demote stock ROCKNIX

In the "UPDATES & DOWNLOADS" > "SOFTWARE UPDATES" menu, add a software-update
action targeting the personal DUCKTALE nightly releases published at
github.com/aanze/distribution (instead of the official update.rocknix.org
endpoint), and make the menu safe to navigate on this fork:

  - The DUCKTALE NIGHTLIES entry is the PRIMARY updater and is listed FIRST. It
    keeps every Ducktale feature.
  - The stock ROCKNIX updater is DEMOTED to the bottom and relabelled
    "UPDATE TO STOCK ROCKNIX (WIPES DUCKTALE)", because selecting it REPLACES
    this Ducktale build with official ROCKNIX and removes all Ducktale features
    -- it is NOT how you keep getting Ducktale nightlies. (APPLY UPDATE is kept
    for the already-staged state.)

Rather than duplicate the whole download/verify/progress/reboot UX, the patch
parameterises the single hardcoded "rocknix-update" command string through the
existing flow:

  - ApiSystem::updateSystem() and ApiSystem::canUpdate() gain an optional
    `updatecommand` argument (default "rocknix-update"), so behaviour for all
    existing callers is unchanged.
  - GuiUpdate (and its inner ThreadedUpdater) gain an optional `updateCommand`
    that is threaded through to canUpdate()/updateSystem().
  - GuiMenu pushes `new GuiUpdate(mWindow, "aanze-update")` for the new entry,
    labelled "DUCKTALE NIGHTLIES" (a product name, shown identically in every
    locale so nothing falls back to an untranslated English string).

GuiUpdate also swaps the confirmation text per path:
  - "aanze-update": a friendly "DUCKTALE NIGHTLY" reminder (every personal build
    carries custom modifications by design, so the stock scare is just noise).
  - "rocknix-update" (stock): an explicit warning that updating to stock ROCKNIX
    REMOVES all Ducktale features, pointing the user back at DUCKTALE NIGHTLIES.
Both reuse the already-translated "YOU ARE CURRENTLY USING VERSION ..." prompt,
so the dialogs stay localized (incl. French) with only the brand/feature lines
in English.

The aanze-update backend script mirrors rocknix-update's contract (`check`
prints the available version and exits 0 when an update is available; the
default mode stages the verified tarball into /storage/.update and returns 0),
so staging + apply-on-reboot via the busybox init updater are identical to the
official path.

